  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'vintage-1960-1970s-old-sterling-silver-ring-morenci-turquoise-hand-stamped-arrow', '4614599369', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/4614599369/vintage-1960-1970s-old-sterling-silver?click_key=3dae72b2-8c6c-4fdc-a727-dda2bfe9b877%3ALT8663d13cd59ad15a2d7b61ab95a824fd9e3407d7&click_sum=87494fa0&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=turquoise+jewelry&ref=search_grid-37503-17-25&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&frs=1&content_source=3dae72b2-8c6c-4fdc-a727-dda2bfe9b877%253ALT8663d13cd59ad15a2d7b61ab95a824fd9e3407d7',
   'Vintage 1960-1970s Old Sterling Silver Ring -Morenci Turquoise, Hand Stamped Arrow Designs, Chunky Statement Ring Size 7.5, 17.5g', 'An exceptional piece of Southwest history, this vintage 1960s–1970s ring features a striking, substantial turquoise cabochon attributed to being Morenci Turquoise. Morenci turquoise comes from the historic Morenci copper mine in Greenlee County, Southeastern Arizona, and is famous for its rich blue color and metallic iron pyrite ("fool''s gold") matrix. All mining operations for Morenci turquoise ceased in 1984 when the lease expired. Because modern copper extraction methods destroy turquoise, all existing material on the market is vintage stock mined prior to 1984. Unsigned and unmarked as was common for the era, the silver has been fully tested and verified as solid sterling silver. The face of the ring boasts a beautiful 1.25-inch turquoise stone. It features a deep water-blue coloration interwoven with a rich brown and tan matrix as well as the striking silver gray pyrite. The stone is set securely in a smooth bezel bordered by a classic, detailed rain-drop/beaded sterling wire edge. The heavy, solid split-shank band features beautiful hand-hammered traditional Native American arrow stamp work on the sides. The silver displays a gorgeous, naturally aged patina that highlights its mid-century craftsmanship. • Era: Circa 1960s - 1970s • Tribal Style: Navajo (Diné) • Metal: Tested Sterling Silver (.925) • Weight: 17.5 Grams (Heavy, solid feel) • Ring Size: 7.5 (US) • Face Dimensions: 1.25" North-to-South 🌿Deeply Rooted • Finely Crafted • Every Piece Holds A Story “We believe that the origins of these handmade crafts; whether tumbled, forged, rolled, or woven, carry their own energy and spirit; their own evolving narrative. Deeply rooted intrinsically, finely crafted through the hands that shape each piece, and the journeys they take through time... Every Piece Holds A Story.” Our Curation Commitment: We do our utmost due diligence to attribute makers, materials, and provenance because authentic Indigenous made art deserves proper attribution. The maker, the traditi', 'turquoise-jewelry',
