  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'alacran-cananea-turquoise-cabochon-mexican-polychrome-trillion-gemstone-28-5-x28', '1485969739', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/1485969739/alacran-turquoise-cabochon-blue-green?click_key=3dae72b2-8c6c-4fdc-a727-dda2bfe9b877%3ALTb76e55243fa4e689a6e1a50a93c4dfdb73956dcc&click_sum=303d3582&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=turquoise+jewelry&ref=search_grid-37503-17-9&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&sts=1&content_source=3dae72b2-8c6c-4fdc-a727-dda2bfe9b877%253ALTb76e55243fa4e689a6e1a50a93c4dfdb73956dcc',
   'Alacran Cananea Turquoise Cabochon: Mexican Polychrome Trillion Gemstone (28.5 x28.8 x29.0 mm, 34.5 carats)', 'This Alacran Turquoise cabochon is a trillion gemstone measuring 28.5 x 28.8 x 29.0 mm and weighing 34.5 carats. The cabochon has an approximate 6.3 mm dome (total height) and a 3.2 mm girdle (side height), making it ideal for a professional bezel setting. The raw material was sourced directly from the mine owner. The Alacran mine is located in the Cananea copper district of Sonora, Mexico, and operates as a small-scale, localized claim with very limited annual production. The turquoise has been professionally stabilized like most turquoise from the area. The gemstone features varying shades of mottled blue-green turquoise and golden-brown host rock matrix along the borders. The material consists of solid turquoise and matrix with no backing material, remaining structurally sound. It has a flat back and a bright luster across the polished surface. Turquoise is a December birthstone, 11th anniversary gemstone and the State Gemstone of Arizona. Metaphysically, turquoise is considered one of the most powerful healing stones. Throughout history different cultures, including Native Americans, Tibetans and Egyptians, revered its healing powers. Turquoise is said to be a stone of communication and also helps the mental state overall by increasing serenity, creativity, empathy, positive thinking, intuition, happiness and wisdom. It is considered a stone of friendship. Its blue color has come to symbolize the spirit or sky. Listing Photo Note: The photos were taken outside in the Arizona sun. Although we strive for color accuracy, computer monitors and cellphone screens may differ; blues are difficult to capture precisely, and reds may appear brighter. Colors may also appear less bright under indoor lighting. The final photo in the photo array is unedited and unaltered except for cropping to a square format, captured directly as the iPhone 17 Pro took it. This untouched photo is included to meet Etsy''s listing authenticity requirements and shows the stone exactly as the came', 'turquoise-jewelry',
