   'Native American Turquoise Coral Bypass Ring Sterling Silver Adjustable Southwestern Ring', 'Beautiful Native American handmade sterling silver bypass ring featuring one oval turquoise cabochon and one oval red coral cabochon. Each stone is individually bezel set and surrounded by detailed hand-applied silverwork, including leaf, floral, scroll, and bead accents. The open bypass design creates a dramatic two-stone presentation while allowing a small amount of flexibility in sizing. This is a substantial little ring with wonderful dimensional silverwork and a classic turquoise-and-coral color combination. Details * Native American made * Sterling silver * Natural turquoise * Red coral * Bypass / wrap-style design * Approximately size 7 as currently shaped * Slightly adjustable due to open design * Weight: approximately 5.45 grams * Two oval cabochons * Detailed floral, leaf, scroll, and bead silverwork * Approximately 1” top-to-bottom face Please review all photographs for measurements, scale, stone characteristics, and overall details. Natural stones may contain variations in color, matrix, and surface characteristics. Production partners WhiteRavenSandS makes this item with help from Native American Artists, United States', 'turquoise-jewelry',
